{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Vendor catalog: what a provider looks like and what to prefill when creating one.",
    "It is the display half. `model_catalog.json` is the wire half -- it answers 'how do I",
    "send a request' by longest-prefix match, and mixing an exact model list into that",
    "matching is how a catch-all entry ends up rendered as a model nobody can select.",
    "",
    "This file never decides behaviour. `registry::create_provider`, `capabilities::resolve`",
    "and `balance::balance_vendor` stay authoritative; `balance` here only keeps a button",
    "off panels where it could do nothing. A test holds the flag to `BalanceVendor`, so the",
    "two cannot drift apart at all.",
    "",
    "`id` is what an account endpoint is keyed on -- `provider_type` cannot be, since every",
    "vendor added after the original five is OpenAI-compatible and they would all be `openai`.",
    "",
    "Moonshot and SiliconFlow each run a mainland site and an international one on separate",
    "accounts whose keys their own docs say are not interchangeable. Only the mainland URL is",
    "prefilled; the other is reached by editing the base URL, and the balance code reads the",
    "host to label the currency because neither reply carries one.",
    "",
    "`auth[]` is a list of objects, not strings, because the endpoint and the dialect belong",
    "to the login method rather than to the vendor: OpenAI's API and ChatGPT's Codex backend",
    "are both `responses`, and a flat default_base_url keyed by format cannot hold both.",
    "",
    "An entry is a creation preset. It is not consulted again once a provider row exists --",
    "a relay URL the user typed is theirs to keep, and a catalog update must never make an",
    "existing configuration illegal.",
    "",
    "Adding a vendor should be this file plus an icon. If it ever needs a Rust change too,",
    "that is the coupling this file exists to remove -- say so in review.",
    "",
    "A single-element `api_formats` means the dialect is not a choice, which is what the UI",
    "reads to omit the selector. Anthropic is the awkward one: its adapter is chosen by",
    "provider_type alone and never reads the column, but the column is NOT NULL DEFAULT",
    "'chat_completions' (migration 10), so that is what its rows actually hold. The value is",
    "inert there rather than descriptive -- do not read it as 'Anthropic speaks OpenAI'."
  ],
  "providers": [
    {
      "id": "openai",
      "provider_type": "openai",
      "name": "OpenAI",
      "icon": "openai",
      "balance": false,
      "websites": {
        "official": "https://openai.com",
        "api_key": "https://platform.openai.com/api-keys",
        "docs": "https://platform.openai.com/docs",
        "models": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/models"
      },
      "auth": [
        {
          "id": "api_key",
          "credential_kind": "api_key",
          "transport_profile": "standard",
          "api_formats": ["chat_completions", "responses"],
          "default_base_url": {
            "chat_completions": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
            "responses": "https://api.openai.com/v1"
          }
        },
        {
